--TEST--
What "The tools you do not install" in the PHP-differences chapter says an analyser and a style checker report is nine compile errors from `nvs check` alone: an unassigned property, a missing visibility, a miscased name, a path that does not return, an unresolved member, an untyped binding, a tainted value at a sink, a `secret` written out and a second spelling — `rule:security/sink-predicate`, `rule:types/conversion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:php-differences/the-tools-you-do-not-install
// What the PHP-differences chapter's "The tools you do not install" says
// `nvs check` reports with no analyser and no style checker installed, one
// line each: a property never assigned, a member with no visibility, a name
// in the wrong case, a path that does not return, a member that does not
// resolve, an untyped binding, a tainted value at a sink, a `secret` written
// out and a second spelling of one operator.
class Cart {
    public int $count;
    int $discount = 0;

    public function Total(): int {
        if ($this->count > 0) {
            return $this->count;
        }
    }

    public function size(): void {
        $this->recount();
    }
}

$lines = 3;
tainted string $name = "guest";
string $content = Core\IO::read($name);
secret string $key = "k" as secret string;
echo $key, "\n";
echo 1 <> 2, "\n";
